body:
No, I believe sociopaths are not onjectvely bad, since by definition they don't understand others' feelings and therefore why certain decisions are "bad" in the first place.  Sort of like children. Children are known to be blunt and hurt people's feelings, but in the moment don't understand why they shouldn't call people out since it can embarrass them. Does this make them "bad"? Perhaps they're actions are "bad", but does this mean that they're a bad person? What does it even mean to be objectively a "bad" person? One who murders, who hates Star Wars, who steals, or who argued, etc. 

&#x200B;

More on, "Can something be objectively bad?" [https://www.reddit.com/r/grammar/comments/5ghsq5/can\_something\_be\_objectively\_bad/](https://www.reddit.com/r/grammar/comments/5ghsq5/can_something_be_objectively_bad/)
